=== spaces and other specials get backslashes
[cd a\ b/][]
[cat it\'s\ here.txt ][]
[cat cost\$1.txt ][]
[cat x\&y.txt ][]
=== a quoted or escaped word completes inside its quotes
[cd "My Documents/][]
[cat "My Documents/report one.txt" ][]
[cat 'My Documents/report one.txt' ][]
[cat 'it'\''s here.txt' ][]
[cat My\ Documents/report\ ][]
[cat My\ Documents/report\ two.txt ][]
[cat "cost\$1.txt" ][]
=== the common part of several matches, without closing the quote
[ls "M][]
[ls My\ Documents/][]
=== case does not have to match, and the line takes the file's case
[cat Readme.md ][]
[cd My\ Documents/][]
[cd Music/][]
[cat readme][]
=== after = only the value is completed
[make --file=Readme.md ][]
[X=Readme.md ][]
[P=/nonexistent:Readme.md ][]
=== the list shows file names without their directory
report one.txt  report two.txt
